        "exposedClass": "review-required",
        "statement": "Certificates signed by CA or SelfSigned issuers with RSA keys of 3072 bits or more now use SHA-384 or SHA-512 signatures, and systems that do not support these hash algorithms may not accept them.",
        "remediation": "If you use an RSA CA key of 3072 bits or more, check that the systems relying on the issued certificates support SHA-384 and SHA-512.",
        "severity": "medium"
